          "text": "Raw attested data is retained in full and never collapsed in the store. Every simplification -- identity, status, confidence, tension, ordering -- is a determined projection computed on demand over that raw data, parameterised by a base the viewer chooses, and therefore swappable: a different base over the same claims yields a different, equally valid view. SPEC section 4.3 states this for identity (M(A,B) as a witness-retaining path-space enriched over the trust structure, so the same SameAs set under a different trust base gives a different identity); the disposable SQLite index, the state fold's poset, and decategorification-only-at-render are the same principle in other places. A field holding a computed value is the failure mode: it asserts an output of the fold as if it were input, and it forecloses every other projection.",
